      "writtenOn": "2022-03-02T00:33:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "All EFS2 systems do the RW jump before power on.  Lazor is proof of concept code only.  Once more herobrine hardware is available we plan to drop lazor support.\n\nI think this change just makes the code more confusing.  It provides multiple paths for the user to specify the power sequence GPIOs.  I hope that once the eSPI VW are wrapped with a GPIO interface, then the power_signals.c only needs to handle two cases: a GPIO pin (direct or IOEX or eSPI VW) and the \"external/custom\"",
      "parentUuid": "474811a5_0e7a9d01",
      "revId": "34561043a8c33e62476195837b4c16f85e6eb403",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6465eea4_2a51d31c",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1281040
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-02T01:43:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Fair enough - I agree that having multiple choices has downsides, and I did go back and forth on whether this was a good thing or not.\nIn some ways it was a proof of concept for the API (whether it could be easily extended to support named-gpios and gpio-interrupts.\n\nBTW, chromium:3482485 adds ADC signal support as well.\n\nThe implication is:\n - any GPIO referenced needs to have the named-gpio instance either removed or have no-auto-init set.\n  - If it gets removed, gpioget/set won\u0027t see it until the upstreamed support for this lands.\n\nThis are easy enough to deal with.",
      "parentUuid": "b3109ef9_ffef93eb",
      "revId": "34561043a8c33e62476195837b4c16f85e6eb403",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "64d0a6c7_d4e7d863",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1361259
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-02T04:00:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`pwrindebug` allows the power inputs to be inspected from the console anyway (so we don\u0027t need gpioget) and I don\u0027t think supporting gpioset is very useful anyway, so it seems simpler to adjust the named-gpios than add these 300 lines of code- and we don\u0027t need to clean it up later.\n\nIf we\u0027re going to carry some amount of technical debt around the legacy GPIO code, I\u0027d rather keep it coupled to the legacy code (attached to legacy-gpios nodes) rather than need to remove it from new Zephyr code later.",
      "parentUuid": "6465eea4_2a51d31c",
      "revId": "34561043a8c33e62476195837b4c16f85e6eb403",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
